{
  "category": "Armor Bird Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Its sturdy wings look heavy, but they are actually hollow and light, allowing it to fly freely in the sky.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "After nesting in bramble bushes, the wings of its chicks grow hard from scratches by thorns.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "The feathers that it sheds are very sharp. It is said that people once used the feathers as swords.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "SKARMORY is entirely encased in hard, protective armor. This POKéMON flies at close to 190 mph. It slashes foes with its wings that possess swordlike cutting edges.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "SKARMORY’s steel wings become tattered and bashed in from repeated battles. Once a year, the battered wings grow back completely, restoring the cutting edges to their pristine state.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "A POKéMON that has a body and wings of steel. People in the past used feathers fallen from SKARMORY to make swords and knives.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "After nesting in bramble bushes, the wings of its chicks grow hard from scratches by thorns.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its sturdy wings look heavy, but its bones are hollow and light, allowing it to fly freely in the sky.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite being clad entirely in iron-hard armor, it flies at speeds over 180 mph.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite being clad entirely in iron-hard armor, it flies at speeds over 180 mph.",
      "version": "pearl"
